# memchentic Tool Routing

Gate: if memchentic is not connected/ready, skip all memchentic tools.

Prefer the smallest tool that answers the question. Default coding turns stay
on recall + capture tools only. Limits default ~20 (search) / ~50 (browse /
since / by_tag), clamped 1–100.

## Everyday (default rules already cover)

| Job | Tool | Params / gotchas |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reusable guides before approach | `guide_find` | `query`; optional `space_id`, `limit`. **Guides only.** Rank = hybrid × confidence. |
| Hybrid search → digests | `find` | `query`; optional `type`, `tags` (**AND**), `space_id`, `path_hint`, `repo_hint`, `limit`. **Entries only** — never returns guides. |
| Full body | `open` | Prefer `id`. Or exact `title` (+ optional `space_id`); first hit across accessible spaces if space omitted. |
| Path-scoped digests | `about_path` | `path`; optional `repo_hint`, `limit`. Matches `path_hint` **or** body text; all kinds. |
| Save durable entry | `remember` | Required `title`, `body`. `type` (default `note`), `tags`, `expires_at` ISO, `path_hint`, `repo_hint`, `force`, write target (`space_id` / `group` / `visibility`). Near-dup refuses unless `force`. |
| Save / strengthen guide | `guide_write` | Required `title`, `body`; optional `tags` + write target. Near-dup **upserts** + confidence += 1. No `force`, type, expiry, or path hints. |
| Patch entry | `revise` | Required `id`. Optional title/body/type/`tags` (**replaces** list)/`expires_at`/`clear_expiry`/path hints. No near-dup check; cannot change space or kind. |

## Situational

| Job | Tool | Params / gotchas |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Who am I / spaces | `me` | Subject, `is_admin`, `personal_space_id`, `default_shared_space_id`, memberships. |
| List spaces | `space_list` | User: memberships. Admin: every unarchived space. |
| Create a group | `space_create` | `name`. Caller becomes creator (roster manager). Any user principal including admin. No name uniqueness. |
| Space detail + members | `space_show` | `space_id`. |
| Paginated list | `browse` | Optional `space_id`, `kind` (`entry`\|`guide`), `type`, `limit`, `offset`. Snippets, newest first; no total count. |
| Time window | `since` | ISO `since` / `until`; filters **`updated_at`**. Optional `space_id`, `limit`. |
| Tag filter | `by_tag` | Required `tags`; `mode` `and` (default) / `or`; optional `space_id`, `limit`. |
| Move memory | `relocate` | Required `id` + destination `space_id` UUID. No `group` / `visibility`. |
| Delete | `forget` | `id` — entry or guide the principal can access. |
| Provenance | `trace` | `id` → kind, created_by, created_at, provenance, space_id. MCP writes store empty provenance. |
| Near-dups / expiry hygiene | `overlap_report` | Optional `space_id`, `limit`. Read-only. Scans newest `OVERLAP_SCAN_LIMIT` (default 2000) rows; pairs are `same_title` or cosine `near_dup`. `conflicts` may be `[]`. Never auto-delete — merge with `revise` / `forget`. |
| Expired rows | recall tools | `find`, `guide_find`, `browse`, `since`, `by_tag`, `about_path` hide past-due `expires_at` by default; pass `include_expired: true` to audit. Hybrid ranking boosts recent, path-tagged, and high-confidence rows. |

## Write target (remember / guide_write)

1. `space_id` → that space.
2. `group` → exact case-insensitive name among the caller’s unarchived groups.
3. `visibility="shared"` → default shared group, else sole group; else error.
4. Else → personal.

`visibility` is `"personal"` or `"shared"`. Default shared group is set via
REST/GUI (`PATCH /api/me`), **not** MCP. Call `me` when unsure.

Admin key = real `ADMIN_EMAIL` user (personal default; may `space_create`).
Prefer per-user key/JWT for agents — admin list/search is instance-wide.

## Entry types (closed)

Pass on `remember` / filter on `find`. Classification only. Default write type
is `note` — pick a better label when one fits (see capture rule).

| Type | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `fact` | Stable truth about the world or codebase |
| `preference` | How someone wants work done |
| `decision` | A choice and its rationale |
| `instruction` | Standing directive the agent should follow |
| `feedback` | Correction after a mistake |
| `insight` | Learned non-obvious finding |
| `note` | Catch-all when nothing else fits |

Guides are not an entry type (`guide_write` / `guide_find`).

## Not on MCP (do not invent tools)

- Set default shared group, roster add/remove, rename/archive group → REST /
  GUI.
- Auth groups, API key management, SSE live events → outside this plugin.

## Explicitly not in v1

Multi-agent queues/leases/meshes, vision search, server-side “reflect the
whole graph,” third-party note-app bridges, and ops diagnose/heal packs.
Grow the **memchentic** surface later when there is a real need — do not
invent foreign tool names.
